steps.description:
Fit a single DESeq2 model on the filtered counts from T1S0 with design ~ condition + time + condition:time, using the actual factor level names read from metadata.csv (control level of `condition` as reference, t0 as reference for `time`). Extract three result tables with independent filtering and BH FDR:
(1) simple treatment effect at t0 — the `condition` main-effect coefficient;
(2) simple treatment effect at t1 — the sum of the condition coefficient and the interaction coefficient, obtained via a contrast list rather than by refitting;
(3) the interaction term itself — the difference of the two treatment effects, which is the direct answer to the research question.
For each table report the number of genes at FDR < 0.05 (and at FDR < 0.10 with |log2FC| > 1 as a secondary, clearly-labelled sensitivity threshold), the top genes by adjusted p-value, and shrunken log2 fold changes (apeglm for the named coefficients, ashr where a contrast list is required) for ranking and plotting. Produce an MA plot and a volcano plot per contrast, and export all three full result tables as CSV with unshrunken and shrunken log2FC, standard error, Wald statistic, raw and adjusted p-value. Also export the VST matrix for the retained genes. State the residual degrees of freedom of the model (12 samples, 4 coefficients => 8 df) and, if the interaction yields few or no significant genes, report that as a power-limited negative rather than as evidence of no time-dependence.

